1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:41,017
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:45,017
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:52,017
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,017 --> 00:02:58,017
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,017 --> 00:03:08,017
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:08,017 --> 00:03:13,017
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:15,017 --> 00:03:23,017
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:30,017
The Fishman Pirates, led by Horty Jones and assisted by Vander Decken, plot to overthrow King Neptune.

9
00:03:30,017 --> 00:03:34,017
It's not long before the Straw Hats get pulled into the conflict.

10
00:03:34,017 --> 00:03:43,017
This will be destroyed. And quickly. We'll rebuild it from scratch. But with a new king. Like me.

11
00:03:43,017 --> 00:03:50,017
Citizens of Fishman Island, the old Ryugu Kingdom has worn out its welcome.

12
00:03:50,017 --> 00:03:53,017
Time to say goodbye.

13
00:03:53,017 --> 00:04:01,017
In three hours, at the Conchcord Plaza, the weak and incompetent King Neptune will be put to death.

14
00:04:01,017 --> 00:04:08,017
Straw Hat, I know. You're there. I have something that may be of interest to you.

15
00:04:08,017 --> 00:04:17,017
As you watch from wherever you are, I want you to know that this is just the beginning of my revenge for what you did to Arla. Enjoy.

16
00:04:17,017 --> 00:04:20,017
Oh man! He even captured Zoro?!

17
00:04:20,017 --> 00:04:22,017
Why do we leave them alone?

18
00:04:22,017 --> 00:04:24,017
But still, all three?

19
00:04:24,017 --> 00:04:27,017
It's water!

20
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:33,017
By the time we finish the king's execution, that room will be completely flooded.

21
00:04:33,017 --> 00:04:40,017
You lowly humans can't survive that, if I'm not mistaken. Too bad.

22
00:04:40,017 --> 00:04:42,017
Hey, Shark! Take me back to the palace!

23
00:04:42,017 --> 00:04:43,017
Yeah!

24
00:04:43,017 --> 00:04:45,017
Luffy! I told you to wait!

25
00:04:45,017 --> 00:04:46,017
Huh?

26
00:04:46,017 --> 00:04:49,017
You don't get it! You people have no business fighting Horden!

27
00:04:49,017 --> 00:04:52,017
You're wrong! Not when my crew's in trouble!

28
00:04:52,017 --> 00:04:56,017
It's not that I don't trust you, but this fight is personal for me, too!

29
00:04:56,017 --> 00:04:58,017
Such a stubborn fool!

30
00:04:58,017 --> 00:05:03,017
You shut up already! If you don't want me to go, then stop me!

31
00:05:03,017 --> 00:05:08,017
Since we were allies before, I had hoped that you would honor my request.

32
00:05:08,017 --> 00:05:14,017
How easily I forget who you are! Hard-headedness truly does run in your family!

33
00:05:16,017 --> 00:05:21,017
Stand down, Luffy! Or else!

34
00:05:21,017 --> 00:05:28,017
The Rift opens up! Luffy vs. Jinbei!

35
00:05:40,017 --> 00:05:45,017
Have I told you what people called me? I was the submarine of the East Blue!

36
00:05:45,017 --> 00:05:49,017
That's cause I could swim an 82-foot pool in no time at all!

37
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:53,017
82 feet? I could run over a pool that tiny!

38
00:05:53,017 --> 00:05:56,017
That's one advantage to being a skeleton! I'm light as air!

39
00:05:58,017 --> 00:06:02,017
You know what? We should have a race one of these days to see which one of us is faster!

40
00:06:02,017 --> 00:06:06,017
Any time you're in the mood to lose, I'll be more than happy to let you eat my dust!

41
00:06:06,017 --> 00:06:10,017
That is if we ever get out of here!

42
00:06:10,017 --> 00:06:12,017
Yeah, this is not looking good for us!

43
00:06:12,017 --> 00:06:15,017
After all that training, crowning is a seriously my way to go!

44
00:06:15,017 --> 00:06:17,017
Anything for a watery grave?

45
00:06:17,017 --> 00:06:19,017
Shut up!

46
00:06:20,017 --> 00:06:23,017
Hey, how is it you can sit there with your eyes closed like nothing's going on?

47
00:06:23,017 --> 00:06:27,017
Oh, I know. You must be coming up with a plan to set us free!

48
00:06:27,017 --> 00:06:28,017
Nope.

49
00:06:28,017 --> 00:06:29,017
You couldn't have lied!

50
00:06:29,017 --> 00:06:31,017
You'll be honest to the bitter end!

51
00:06:31,017 --> 00:06:32,017
Wow!

52
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:36,017
Everything would be fine if I had a sword!

53
00:06:36,017 --> 00:06:37,017
I don't think that's true.

54
00:06:38,017 --> 00:06:40,017
Things have gotten bleak.

55
00:06:41,017 --> 00:06:44,017
I didn't want to do this in front of you, but so be it.

56
00:06:44,017 --> 00:06:46,017
Uh, do what exactly?

57
00:06:53,017 --> 00:06:55,017
Okay, Brook, you're really starting to freak me out here!

58
00:06:59,017 --> 00:07:01,017
Stop! That's enough!

59
00:07:02,017 --> 00:07:03,017
No!

60
00:07:09,017 --> 00:07:10,017
Kaboom!

61
00:07:11,017 --> 00:07:12,017
And I'm out!

62
00:07:17,017 --> 00:07:20,017
Well, good luck, you guys!

63
00:07:20,017 --> 00:07:21,017
Wait a damn second!

64
00:07:21,017 --> 00:07:22,017
Huh?

65
00:07:22,017 --> 00:07:24,017
You're just gonna leave without explaining or anything?

66
00:07:24,017 --> 00:07:27,017
Since when have you been able to do something like this freaky crap?

67
00:07:27,017 --> 00:07:31,017
What? You mean make my soul leave my body?

68
00:07:31,017 --> 00:07:34,017
Yeah, I thought only real dead people did that!

69
00:07:34,017 --> 00:07:35,017
It's a new trick.

70
00:07:35,017 --> 00:07:36,017
I was surprised.

71
00:07:36,017 --> 00:07:40,017
It first happened on my world tour as Soul King quite suddenly.

72
00:07:42,017 --> 00:07:45,017
During that time, I had fallen into a dreadful slump.

73
00:07:46,017 --> 00:07:49,017
The sales of my TDs and concert tickets were on the decline.

74
00:07:49,017 --> 00:07:52,017
I wasn't sure what I should do to stay relevant.

75
00:07:52,017 --> 00:07:53,017
Bummer.

76
00:07:53,017 --> 00:07:55,017
Today's show wasn't groovy at all, was it?

77
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:59,017
Hate to say it, but I liked his old music better.

78
00:07:59,017 --> 00:08:02,017
It's like, I don't feel his soul anymore.

79
00:08:02,017 --> 00:08:04,017
What the hell's happening to you, Brooke?

80
00:08:04,017 --> 00:08:07,017
If you don't write a song that sells, I'm cutting you loose!

81
00:08:08,017 --> 00:08:10,017
I'm trying, I promise.

82
00:08:10,017 --> 00:08:12,017
But it's not that easy.

83
00:08:13,017 --> 00:08:16,017
Music isn't something you simply throw together.

84
00:08:17,017 --> 00:08:23,017
Maybe I'm forsaken, and the god of music doesn't smile upon me anymore.

85
00:08:23,017 --> 00:08:27,017
I beg of you, let me write one last good song.

86
00:08:27,017 --> 00:08:28,017
Oh, please.

87
00:08:29,017 --> 00:08:31,017
Bless me, god of music.

88
00:08:31,017 --> 00:08:34,017
Grant me a melody that will shake all who hear it to their souls.

89
00:08:35,017 --> 00:08:36,017
Please.

90
00:08:36,017 --> 00:08:38,017
What's going on?!

91
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:45,017
It was frightening at first, but it really helped.

92
00:08:45,017 --> 00:08:48,017
With this new ability came an epiphany.

93
00:08:48,017 --> 00:09:03,017
I finally realized what was missing from my music and how to get out of my slump.

94
00:09:03,017 --> 00:09:05,457
to get out of my slum, which was...

95
00:09:05,457 --> 00:09:12,457
Well, it's actually pretty obvious

96
00:09:12,457 --> 00:09:13,597
when you think about it.

97
00:09:13,877 --> 00:09:15,817
If a man can go anywhere undetected,

98
00:09:16,737 --> 00:09:19,337
there's one thing he's going to go looking for.

99
00:09:20,337 --> 00:09:21,697
He's so lucky, Zoro.

100
00:09:21,897 --> 00:09:23,897
Why can't I be dead like he is?

101
00:09:24,017 --> 00:09:24,417
Really?

102
00:09:26,097 --> 00:09:28,497
Hey, the water's gotten so high,

103
00:09:28,577 --> 00:09:29,977
soon you will be dead like me.

104
00:09:30,037 --> 00:09:31,817
You just had to remind me, didn't you?

105
00:09:31,817 --> 00:09:33,377
Hurry up and do something!

106
00:09:44,817 --> 00:09:47,037
Please, you two, try to calm down.

107
00:09:47,477 --> 00:09:48,757
Luffy! Jinbei!

108
00:09:49,197 --> 00:09:51,117
This is no time for you guys to act like

109
00:09:51,117 --> 00:09:52,377
you're going to kill each other!

110
00:09:52,577 --> 00:09:55,317
Get out of my way! I gotta go save my friends!

111
00:09:55,417 --> 00:09:57,677
And when I'm done, I'm kicking Hordy's ass!

112
00:09:57,757 --> 00:09:59,937
I told you not to get involved with him, Luffy!

113
00:09:59,937 --> 00:10:02,197
Whoa, hey, surely there's a better way

114
00:10:02,197 --> 00:10:02,997
