Active hope for the original faxure.

205
00:14:06,997 --> 00:14:07,857
When the battle stopped again, it won't lose.

206
00:14:07,857 --> 00:14:09,997
Action and patience is alreadyphones

207
00:14:09,997 --> 00:14:11,837
The last big zear.

208
00:14:11,837 --> 00:14:13,377
delight in elters

209
00:14:13,377 --> 00:14:14,037
mushed

210
00:14:14,037 --> 00:14:18,037
Damn it! How'd we lose?

211
00:14:24,037 --> 00:14:27,037
Yeah! I never doubted the three royal brothers for a second!

212
00:14:27,037 --> 00:14:29,037
Thank you, Prince Fugaboshi!

213
00:14:29,037 --> 00:14:32,037
My lord, please leave the rest to us.

214
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:37,037
Much appreciated. We must hurry to Conchcord Plaza in order to prevent our father's execution.

215
00:14:39,037 --> 00:14:42,037
All right, let's go!

216
00:14:44,037 --> 00:14:50,037
Well, it's about time we got this show underway.

217
00:14:50,037 --> 00:14:55,037
Do you want some of us to stay and protect the palace while you're gone, Boss Horty?

218
00:14:55,037 --> 00:14:58,037
No need. But don't you remember?

219
00:14:58,037 --> 00:15:01,037
No one else can get through the palace gate.

220
00:15:01,037 --> 00:15:06,037
We'll station a handful of men here to make sure someone's around to open it when I return.

221
00:15:06,037 --> 00:15:08,037
After all, you can't lock out the new king.

222
00:15:08,037 --> 00:15:11,037
That'd be a shame!

223
00:15:11,037 --> 00:15:13,037
More like nonsense.

224
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:18,037
You will never be respected as king if you rule through violence.

225
00:15:19,037 --> 00:15:23,037
Is that really what you want your last words to be? I'd have gone for something strong.

226
00:15:23,037 --> 00:15:33,037
My scar, it's burning. I can't believe that stupid human swordsman actually managed to cut me.

227
00:15:33,037 --> 00:15:37,037
It's wearing off. Hey, it's time for my next dose.

228
00:15:37,037 --> 00:15:53,037
Now I feel as good as new. Isn't it dangerous taking that much at once?

229
00:15:53,037 --> 00:15:54,037
I thought so.

230
00:15:54,037 --> 00:15:58,037
Hey, Captain. What do we do with the three straw hats we captured?

231
00:15:58,037 --> 00:16:07,037
Nothing. They're just humans. They'll drown if left alone. And the palace is secure so no one will be able to rescue them regardless of who comes.

232
00:16:07,037 --> 00:16:13,037
Forget them. Now what's the current status of the residents from the fishman district that we recruited today?

233
00:16:13,037 --> 00:16:19,037
They're doing just fine. In fact, they should be making their move as we speak.

234
00:16:19,037 --> 00:16:31,037
That's good. Pretty soon they'll be out of the slums. Seeing as once all of the traitors have left or been killed, there'll be plenty of houses on the market.

235
00:16:31,037 --> 00:16:40,037
Then our country will finally be united in its hatred for the pathetic human race.

236
00:16:44,037 --> 00:16:47,037
I think I found it, guys. A bright ray of hope.

237
00:16:47,037 --> 00:16:53,037
Listen, those fishmen we were dealing with earlier have left so the palace is completely empty.

238
00:16:53,037 --> 00:16:56,037
Or rather, it would be if they hadn't left Papagu behind.

239
00:16:56,037 --> 00:17:00,037
That's awesome, Brooke. Now we just need to ask Papagu to find the keys to get us out of these chains.

240
00:17:00,037 --> 00:17:03,037
I guess we need the one to unlock this cage, too.

241
00:17:03,037 --> 00:17:09,037
Don't be an idiot. Just find one of my swords. That's all we really need to escape.

242
00:17:10,037 --> 00:17:12,037
I'll cut anything in my way.

243
00:17:12,037 --> 00:17:14,037
Yeah! That's all you ever want to do!

244
00:17:14,037 --> 00:17:17,037
All right! I'm off to search for Papagu!

245
00:17:17,037 --> 00:17:19,037
Yo-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

246
00:17:19,037 --> 00:17:35,037
I am freaking out! Why did this have to happen? Come have a banquet, they said. It'll be fun!

247
00:17:36,037 --> 00:17:38,037
I hope the straw hats are okay.

248
00:17:38,037 --> 00:17:40,037
I am the only one who's ready.

249
00:17:40,037 --> 00:17:41,037
Ah!

250
00:17:41,037 --> 00:17:43,037
PAPA GU!

251
00:17:43,037 --> 00:17:44,037
No!

252
00:17:44,037 --> 00:17:45,037
No!

253
00:17:45,037 --> 00:17:46,037
No!

254
00:17:46,037 --> 00:17:47,037
No!

255
00:17:47,037 --> 00:17:48,037
